    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1422">

                <pb facs="1142" n="1132" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.4556/7–1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Callanan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-15">July 15, 1949.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 15—7:01 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>210. Director Foreign Affairs Bureau summoned Pao<anchor n="75" xml:id="d1422-f1"
                    /> his office this morning and verbally gave order issued by WMCC<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d1422-f2"/> to stop all functions USIS<anchor n="77"
                        xml:id="d1422-f3"/> 1 p. m. today. No reasons for action given other than
                    military situation. Copy of order refused but USIS interpreter allowed on
                    request take down order as dictated. Order observed but will endeavor arrange
                    resume some functions. Complete details upcoming.<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d1422-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 210, repeated Nanking 166, OffEmb Canton 99.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Callanan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1422-f1" n="75" xml:id="d1422-f1-content">
                <p>Chinese news editor of USIS.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1422-f2" n="76" xml:id="d1422-f2-content">
                <p>Wuhan Military Control Commission.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1422-f3" n="77" xml:id="d1422-f3-content">
                <p>United States Information Service.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1422-f4" n="78" xml:id="d1422-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 211, July 16, from the Consul General at Hankow, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
